{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And the nazirite shall shave at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting.</b> One might think he shaves in the courtyard — that would be a disgrace. Rather, ״and the nazirite shall shave״ is after the slaughter of the shelamim offerings, for it is written of them ״וּשְׁחָטוֹ פֶּתַח אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד״." "<b>That is under the slaughter of the shelamim.</b> Under the pot in which it is cooked — for the shelamim of a nazirite were cooked in the courtyard, since the priest must take the foreleg after it has been cooked and wave it before YHWH (see Nazir 45)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:42.785723189Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}